From b6f2eb9a5411e2a353357b4731b93d536681237f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:13:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - free the fallback if cipher initialization
 fails

The software fallback is allocated before the SA record. If the latter
allocation fails, cra_init returns without releasing the fallback; the
Crypto API does not call cra_exit for a failed initialization.

Free the fallback before returning ENOMEM. crypto_free_skcipher() also
accepts NULL for algorithms which do not allocate a fallback.

Signed-off-by: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
---
 eip93-cipher.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/eip93-cipher.c b/eip93-cipher.c
index 82d1a1d..9ce90bb 100644
--- a/eip93-cipher.c
+++ b/eip93-cipher.c
@@ -62,8 +62,10 @@ static int eip93_skcipher_cra_init(struct crypto_tfm *tfm)
 	ctx->type = tmpl->type;
 
 	ctx->sa_record = kzalloc(sizeof(*ctx->sa_record), GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (!ctx->sa_record)
+	if (!ctx->sa_record) {
+		crypto_free_skcipher(ctx->fallback);
 		return -ENOMEM;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
